---
import PrayerText from '../../../components/PrayerText.astro';
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { prayerLines } from '../../../lib/content';
import { bars, beats, range, tempo } from '../../../lib/manto';

const path = '/es/laboratorio/melodia-del-manto/';
const hailMary = prayerLines('hail-mary', 'es');
const score = JSON.stringify({ beats, range, tempo });
---

<Base
  language="es"
  title="La melodía del manto"
  description="Un experimento: la melodía que Fernando Ojeda lee en las estrellas y las flores de la imagen de la Virgen de Guadalupe, tocada y dibujada nota por nota."
  alternates={{ en: '/', es: path }}
  noindex
>
  <section class="wrap narrow page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Laboratorio · devoción</p>
    <h1>La melodía del manto</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Las 46 estrellas del manto y las flores de la túnica de la Virgen de Guadalupe, leídas como notas
      sobre un teclado. Toca para escucharla mientras se dibuja.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap stage-wrap" aria-label="Melodía y animación">
    <figure class="stage">
      <canvas id="manto" role="img" aria-label="Las estrellas de la melodía aparecen de abajo arriba sobre un teclado, una por cada nota."></canvas>
      <figcaption class="now" aria-live="polite"><span id="now">Prueba 2 · de los pies a la cabeza</span></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="controls">
      <button id="play" class="button is-solid play" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
        <span class="play-label">Escuchar</span>
      </button>
      <fieldset class="tempo">
        <legend class="visually-hidden">Ritmo</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name="tempo" value="score" checked /><span>Partitura</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="tempo" value="double" /><span>Doble tiempo</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="tempo" value="prayer" /><span>Para rezar</span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <label class="volume">
        <span>Volumen</span>
        <input id="volume" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.7" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <p class="hint" id="tempo-hint">
      La partitura va a 75 negras por minuto, nota por nota, como la imprime Ojeda.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow pray" aria-labelledby="pray-title">
    <h2 id="pray-title">Rezar una decena con la melodía de fondo</h2>
    <p>
      Elige "Para rezar": la melodía se alarga, baja de volumen y se repite sin fin. Avanza las
      Avemarías a tu paso.
    </p>
    <div class="bead-card">
      <div class="beads" aria-hidden="true">
        {Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, index) => <span class="bead" data-bead={index}></span>)}
      </div>
      <p class="count" id="count" aria-live="polite">Avemaría 1 de 10</p>
      <PrayerText text={hailMary} lang="es" />
      <div class="bead-actions">
        <button id="bead-back" class="button" type="button">Anterior</button>
        <button id="bead-next" class="button is-solid" type="button">Siguiente</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h2 id="about-title">Qué es</h2>
    <p>
      El investigador yucateco Fernando Ojeda Llanes propuso que la imagen de la Virgen de Guadalupe
      guarda una melodía. Dibujó la imagen dentro de un rectángulo áureo, trazó una línea vertical por
      el centro y 23 a cada lado, una por cada una de las 46 estrellas, y puso encima el teclado de un
      piano con el do central en la línea del centro. Cada línea y cada espacio es una tecla blanca.
      Cada estrella y el centro de cada flor de la túnica se vuelven una nota, leídas por renglones.
    </p>
    <p>
      Es una lectura devocional y personal. La Iglesia venera la imagen y celebra su fiesta el 12 de
      diciembre; sobre esta música no se ha pronunciado. Alberto Aguilar Portillo, el músico que la
      arregló, la describe en el libro como "un ejercicio de libre interpretación".
    </p>

    <h3>Cómo suena aquí</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li>
        Las notas son las de la "Prueba 2, registros centrales" de su libro: de los pies a la cabeza,
        en el registro medio del piano, {bars.length} compases de 4/4.
      </li>
      <li>
        El sonido se genera en tu navegador con un timbre de cuerdas suave. No usa sus grabaciones,
        que tienen todos los derechos reservados.
      </li>
      <li>
        Los acordes de los compases 5 a 8 se leyeron de una copia escaneada y faltan por cotejar con
        la grabación original.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Para conocer más</h3>
    <ul class="links">
      <li>
        <a href="https://fernandoojeda.com/musica-en-la-imagen-de-la-virgen-de-guadalupe/" rel="noopener">
          Música en la imagen de la Virgen de Guadalupe
        </a>, el estudio en el sitio de Fernando Ojeda
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://fernandoojeda.com/audios/" rel="noopener">Sus grabaciones</a>: piano, arpa, cuarteto, coro
        y orquesta
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://fernandoojeda.com/las-constelaciones-en-la-imagen-de-la-virgen-de-guadalupe/" rel="noopener">
          Las constelaciones en la imagen
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ score }}>
  (function () {
    var data = JSON.parse(score);
    var canvas = document.getElementById('manto');
    var context = canvas.getContext('2d');
    var playButton = document.getElementById('play');
    var playLabel = playButton.querySelector('.play-label');
    var nowLabel = document.getElementById('now');
    var hint = document.getElementById('tempo-hint');
    var volumeInput = document.getElementById('volume');
    var reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    var letters = ['C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'A', 'B'];
    var semitones = [0, 2, 4, 5, 7, 9, 11];
    var names = { C: 'do', D: 're', E: 'mi', F: 'fa', G: 'sol', A: 'la', B: 'si' };
    function stepOf(note) {
      return (Number(note.slice(1)) - 4) * 7 + letters.indexOf(note[0]);
    }
    function frequencyOf(note) {
      var midi = 12 * (Number(note.slice(1)) + 1) + semitones[letters.indexOf(note[0])];
      return 440 * Math.pow(2, (midi - 69) / 12);
    }

    var modes = {
      score: { beat: 60 / data.tempo, attack: 0.04, release: 0.9, level: 0.16, cutoff: 3200, loop: false,
        hint: 'La partitura va a 75 negras por minuto, nota por nota, como la imprime Ojeda.' },
      double: { beat: 120 / data.tempo, attack: 0.12, release: 1.8, level: 0.15, cutoff: 2600, loop: false,
        hint: 'Al doble de tiempo, como la "Armonía Original" que grabó con instrumentos electrónicos.' },
      prayer: { beat: 4.2, attack: 1.6, release: 7, level: 0.1, cutoff: 1400, loop: true,
        hint: 'Muy lenta y baja, en bucle: un fondo para rezar sin que la melodía pida atención.' },
    };
    var mode = modes.score;

    // Each star sits on its key's line; beats climb from the feet to the head, as Prueba 2 reads.
    var stars = [];
    data.beats.forEach(function (beat, index) {
      beat.forEach(function (note, voice) {
        stars.push({ note: note, beat: index, step: stepOf(note), voice: voice, seed: Math.sin(index * 12.9898 + voice * 78.233) });
      });
    });
    var total = data.beats.length;

    var audio = null;
    var playing = false;
    var startTime = 0;
    var nextBeat = 0;
    var scheduled = [];
    var timer = null;
    var lit = new Map();

    function makeImpulse(ctx, seconds) {
      var length = Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds);
      var impulse = ctx.createBuffer(2, length, ctx.sampleRate);
      for (var channel = 0; channel < 2; channel++) {
        var samples = impulse.getChannelData(channel);
        for (var i = 0; i < length; i++) {
          samples[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * Math.pow(1 - i / length, 3.2);
        }
      }
      return impulse;
    }

    function setupAudio() {
      var ctx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
      var master = ctx.createGain();
      master.gain.value = Number(volumeInput.value);
      var compressor = ctx.createDynamicsCompressor();
      compressor.threshold.value = -18;
      compressor.ratio.value = 3;
      var reverb = ctx.createConvolver();
      reverb.buffer = makeImpulse(ctx, 4.5);
      var wet = ctx.createGain();
      wet.gain.value = 0.55;
      var dry = ctx.createGain();
      dry.gain.value = 0.6;
      var bus = ctx.createGain();
      bus.connect(dry);
      bus.connect(reverb);
      reverb.connect(wet);
      dry.connect(compressor);
      wet.connect(compressor);
      compressor.connect(master);
      master.connect(ctx.destination);
      return { ctx: ctx, master: master, bus: bus };
    }

    function voice(note, at, length, chordSize) {
      var ctx = audio.ctx;
      var frequency = frequencyOf(note);
      var level = mode.level / Math.sqrt(chordSize);
      var envelope = ctx.createGain();
      var filter = ctx.createBiquadFilter();
      filter.type = 'lowpass';
      filter.frequency.value = mode.cutoff;
      filter.Q.value = 0.4;
      envelope.gain.setValueAtTime(0, at);
      envelope.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(level, at + mode.attack);
      envelope.gain.setTargetAtTime(level * 0.7, at + mode.attack, length * 0.5);
      envelope.gain.setTargetAtTime(0, at + length, mode.release / 4);
      filter.connect(envelope);
      envelope.connect(audio.bus);
      var end = at + length + mode.release * 1.5;
      [-6, 6].forEach(function (cents) {
        var oscillator = ctx.createOscillator();
        oscillator.type = 'sawtooth';
        oscillator.frequency.value = frequency;
        oscillator.detune.value = cents;
        var gain = ctx.createGain();
        gain.gain.value = 0.32;
        oscillator.connect(gain);
        gain.connect(filter);
        oscillator.start(at);
        oscillator.stop(end);
      });
      var body = ctx.createOscillator();
      body.type = 'sine';
      body.frequency.value = frequency / 2;
      var bodyGain = ctx.createGain();
      bodyGain.gain.value = 0.35;
      body.connect(bodyGain);
      bodyGain.connect(filter);
      body.start(at);
      body.stop(end);
    }

    function schedule() {
      var ctx = audio.ctx;
      while (startTime + nextBeat * mode.beat < ctx.currentTime + 0.4) {
        var index = nextBeat % (total + 1);
        var at = startTime + nextBeat * mode.beat;
        if (index < total) {
          var beat = data.beats[index];
          beat.forEach(function (note) {
            voice(note, at, mode.beat * (mode.loop ? 1.6 : 0.95), beat.length);
          });
          scheduled.push({ at: at, index: index });
        } else if (!mode.loop) {
          scheduled.push({ at: at, index: -1 });
          nextBeat++;
          break;
        }
        nextBeat++;
      }
    }

    function start() {
      if (audio === null) {
        audio = setupAudio();
      }
      void audio.ctx.resume();
      startTime = audio.ctx.currentTime + 0.15;
      nextBeat = 0;
      scheduled = [];
      lit.clear();
      playing = true;
      schedule();
      timer = window.setInterval(schedule, 100);
      playButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
      playLabel.textContent = 'Pausar';
    }

    function stop() {
      playing = false;
      window.clearInterval(timer);
      if (audio !== null) {
        var ctx = audio.ctx;
        audio.master.gain.setTargetAtTime(0, ctx.currentTime, 0.3);
        var old = audio;
        audio = null;
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          void old.ctx.close();
        }, 1500);
      }
      playButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
      playLabel.textContent = 'Escuchar';
    }

    playButton.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (playing) {
        stop();
      } else {
        start();
      }
    });

    document.querySelectorAll('input[name="tempo"]').forEach(function (input) {
      input.addEventListener('change', function () {
        mode = modes[input.value];
        hint.textContent = mode.hint;
        if (playing) {
          stop();
          start();
        }
      });
    });

    volumeInput.addEventListener('input', function () {
      if (audio !== null) {
        audio.master.gain.setTargetAtTime(Number(volumeInput.value), audio.ctx.currentTime, 0.05);
      }
    });

    // Drawing.
    var width = 0;
    var height = 0;
    var palette = {};
    function readPalette() {
      var style = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
      palette = {
        ink: style.getPropertyValue('--ink').trim(),
        mute: style.getPropertyValue('--mute').trim(),
        line: style.getPropertyValue('--line').trim(),
        gold: style.getPropertyValue('--gold').trim(),
        accent: style.getPropertyValue('--accent').trim(),
        light: document.documentElement.dataset.theme === 'light',
      };
    }

    function resize() {
      var ratio = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
      var rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
      width = rect.width;
      height = rect.height;
      canvas.width = Math.round(width * ratio);
      canvas.height = Math.round(height * ratio);
      context.setTransform(ratio, 0, 0, ratio, 0, 0);
    }

    function star(x, y, radius, points, rotation) {
      context.beginPath();
      for (var i = 0; i < points * 2; i++) {
        var angle = rotation + (i * Math.PI) / points;
        var r = i % 2 === 0 ? radius : radius * 0.42;
        context.lineTo(x + Math.cos(angle) * r, y + Math.sin(angle) * r);
      }
      context.closePath();
    }

    function geometry() {
      // The golden frame Ojeda draws: 12.60 by 20.39 cm.
      var frameHeight = Math.min(height - 72, (width - 32) * (20.39 / 12.6));
      var frameWidth = frameHeight * (12.6 / 20.39);
      var left = (width - frameWidth) / 2;
      var top = 64;
      var keys = data.range.high - data.range.low + 1;
      return { left: left, top: top, width: frameWidth, height: frameHeight, keys: keys, keyWidth: frameWidth / keys };
    }

    function xOf(g, step) {
      return g.left + (step - data.range.low + 0.5) * g.keyWidth;
    }

    function yOf(g, beat) {
      var inner = g.height - 36;
      return g.top + 18 + inner - (beat / (total - 1)) * inner;
    }

    function draw(time) {
      var g = geometry();
      context.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);
      var now = audio !== null ? audio.ctx.currentTime : 0;
      var current = -1;
      for (var s = scheduled.length - 1; s >= 0; s--) {
        if (scheduled[s].at <= now) {
          current = scheduled[s].index;
          if (current >= 0 && !lit.has(scheduled[s].at)) {
            if (current === 0) {
              lit.clear();
            }
            lit.set(scheduled[s].at, current);
          }
          break;
        }
      }
      if (current === -1 && playing && scheduled.length > 0 && scheduled[scheduled.length - 1].index === -1 && scheduled[scheduled.length - 1].at <= now) {
        stop();
      }
      var breathing = reduceMotion ? 0.5 : 0.5 + 0.5 * Math.sin(time / 2400);

      // Rays around the frame, the aureole of the image.
      context.save();
      var cx = g.left + g.width / 2;
      var cy = g.top + g.height / 2;
      context.strokeStyle = palette.gold;
      context.lineWidth = 1;
      for (var r = 0; r < 120; r++) {
        var angle = (r / 120) * Math.PI * 2;
        var inner = 0.5 + 0.03 * Math.sin(r * 3.1);
        var rx = (g.width / 2) * 1.06;
        var ry = (g.height / 2) * 1.02;
        context.globalAlpha = (palette.light ? 0.18 : 0.12) + 0.08 * breathing * ((r % 3) / 2);
        context.beginPath();
        context.moveTo(cx + Math.cos(angle) * rx * inner, cy + Math.sin(angle) * ry * inner);
        context.lineTo(cx + Math.cos(angle) * rx, cy + Math.sin(angle) * ry);
        context.stroke();
      }
      context.restore();

      // Frame and key lines: every line and every space is a white key.
      context.save();
      context.strokeStyle = palette.line;
      context.lineWidth = 1;
      context.strokeRect(g.left, g.top, g.width, g.height);
      for (var k = 0; k < g.keys; k++) {
        var step = data.range.low + k;
        var x = xOf(g, step);
        context.globalAlpha = step === 0 ? 0.9 : step % 2 === 0 ? 0.55 : 0.2;
        context.strokeStyle = step === 0 ? palette.accent : palette.line;
        context.beginPath();
        context.moveTo(x, g.top);
        context.lineTo(x, g.top + g.height);
        context.stroke();
      }
      context.restore();

      // The keyboard on top, lit by what sounds now.
      var activeSteps = new Set();
      if (current >= 0) {
        data.beats[current].forEach(function (note) {
          activeSteps.add(stepOf(note));
        });
      }
      for (var key = 0; key < g.keys; key++) {
        var keyStep = data.range.low + key;
        var kx = g.left + key * g.keyWidth;
        context.fillStyle = activeSteps.has(keyStep) ? palette.gold : palette.light ? '#fffaf2' : '#e9e2d4';
        context.globalAlpha = activeSteps.has(keyStep) ? 1 : palette.light ? 1 : 0.9;
        context.fillRect(kx + 0.5, g.top - 40, g.keyWidth - 1, 34);
        context.globalAlpha = 1;
        // Black keys between C-D, D-E, F-G, G-A, A-B.
        var letter = ((keyStep % 7) + 7) % 7;
        if (key < g.keys - 1 && letter !== 2 && letter !== 6) {
          context.fillStyle = palette.light ? '#1d1a16' : '#0a0e17';
          context.fillRect(kx + g.keyWidth * 0.68, g.top - 40, g.keyWidth * 0.64, 20);
        }
      }

      // Stars: dim until they sound, then they stay lit.
      var litBeats = new Set(lit.values());
      stars.forEach(function (item) {
        var sx = xOf(g, item.step);
        var sy = yOf(g, item.beat);
        var isNow = item.beat === current;
        var wasLit = litBeats.has(item.beat);
        var size = Math.max(4, g.keyWidth * 0.32);
        var twinkle = reduceMotion ? 0 : Math.sin(time / 700 + item.seed * 40) * 0.12;
        if (isNow) {
          context.save();
          var glow = context.createRadialGradient(sx, sy, 0, sx, sy, size * 5);
          glow.addColorStop(0, palette.gold);
          glow.addColorStop(1, 'transparent');
          context.globalAlpha = 0.45;
          context.fillStyle = glow;
          context.fillRect(sx - size * 5, sy - size * 5, size * 10, size * 10);
          context.globalAlpha = 0.5;
          context.strokeStyle = palette.gold;
          context.beginPath();
          context.moveTo(sx, sy);
          context.lineTo(sx, g.top);
          context.stroke();
          context.restore();
        }
        context.save();
        context.globalAlpha = isNow ? 1 : wasLit ? 0.85 + twinkle : 0.16;
        context.fillStyle = wasLit || isNow ? palette.gold : palette.mute;
        star(sx, sy, isNow ? size * 1.5 : size, 8, item.seed + (reduceMotion ? 0 : time / 9000));
        context.fill();
        context.restore();
      });

      if (current >= 0) {
        var label = data.beats[current]
          .map(function (note) {
            return names[note[0]];
          })
          .join(' · ');
        var bar = Math.floor(current / 4) + 1;
        if (nowLabel.dataset.beat !== String(current)) {
          nowLabel.dataset.beat = String(current);
          nowLabel.textContent = 'Compás ' + bar + ' · ' + label;
        }
      }
      window.requestAnimationFrame(draw);
    }

    readPalette();
    resize();
    window.addEventListener('resize', resize);
    new MutationObserver(readPalette).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-theme'] });
    window.requestAnimationFrame(draw);

    // A decade prayed at one's own pace over the music.
    var bead = 0;
    var beadEls = document.querySelectorAll('.bead');
    var count = document.getElementById('count');
    function renderBeads() {
      beadEls.forEach(function (el, index) {
        el.classList.toggle('done', index < bead);
        el.classList.toggle('current', index === bead);
      });
      count.textContent = bead >= 10 ? 'Gloria al Padre' : 'Avemaría ' + (bead + 1) + ' de 10';
    }
    document.getElementById('bead-next').addEventListener('click', function () {
      bead = Math.min(10, bead + 1);
      renderBeads();
    });
    document.getElementById('bead-back').addEventListener('click', function () {
      bead = Math.max(0, bead - 1);
      renderBeads();
    });
    renderBeads();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .stage-wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    justify-items: center;
  }

  .stage {
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 560px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  canvas {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 12.6 / 22.4;
    max-height: 82vh;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 55%, color-mix(in srgb, #2c6b66 30%, transparent), transparent 70%),
      var(--bg-deep);
  }

  .now {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--mute);
    min-height: 1.6em;
  }

  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .play {
    min-width: 9rem;
  }

  .tempo {
    display: flex;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 3px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tempo label {
    position: relative;
  }

  .tempo input {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    inset: 0;
    margin: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .tempo span {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--mute);
  }

  .tempo input:checked + span {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .tempo input:focus-visible + span {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .volume {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--mute);
  }

  .volume input {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
    width: 8rem;
  }

  .hint {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .pray,
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-5) 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .about {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .bead-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .beads {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .bead {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
